                                                        <script>
                                                            const faqData = {
                                                                general: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is game porting?",
                                                                        a: "Game porting is the process of adapting an existing game from its original platform to a new target platform by reworking engine configuration, SDK integration, control scheme, performance profile, and UI to meet the player expectations of the destination platform."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How is game porting different from remaking a game?",
                                                                        a: "A port adapts the existing game's codebase and assets to run on a new platform by preserving the core gameplay, art, and content while reworking the technical implementation for the target environment. A remake rebuilds the game with new assets, a new engine, or significant design changes."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is cross-platform game development?",
                                                                        a: "Cross-platform game development is building a title from the ground up to run on multiple platforms from a single shared codebase by using platform-specific build configurations, input abstraction layers, and systems that allow one production pipeline to target iOS, Android, PC, and console simultaneously."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What platforms does Clarisco's game porting studio support?",
                                                                        a: "Our game porting services cover PlayStation 5, Xbox Series X|S, Nintendo Switch (handheld and docked), iOS, Android, Steam (PC), and WebGL, with cross-play integration available for titles targeting simultaneous multiplayer across multiple platforms."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Why should I use an external game porting company rather than porting in-house?",
                                                                        a: "External game porting companies keep your internal engineering team on your primary development roadmap rather than context-switching into a six-month platform certification cycle. Our porting team's dedicated focus and existing certification experience also reduce the time and first-submission failure risk."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What makes Clarisco a reliable game porting company for indie studios?",
                                                                        a: "Clarisco's porting practice is specifically sized to serve indie studios with transparent game porting cost estimates, fixed-scope engagement options, and certification management handled by our team so indie studios access platform expertise they couldn't build internally for a single title."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Does Clarisco handle porting for both Unity and Unreal Engine titles?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our game porting studio handles Unity cross-platform development and porting and Unreal Engine cross-platform porting with engine-specific expertise covering Unity's platform build pipeline and UE5's scalability and SDK integration framework per target platform."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is the most technically difficult platform to port to?",
                                                                        a: "Nintendo Switch is consistently the most technically demanding port destination due to its constrained memory (4GB), lower GPU performance, thermal management requirements, and the shader compilation stutter problem that requires specific pre-compilation solutions."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],
                                                                business: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What does a PC to console porting engagement with Clarisco include?",
                                                                        a: "A PC-to-console porting engagement includes technical assessment, SDK integration, platform feature implementation, UI adaptation for TV display, controller UX redesign, performance optimization to platform frame rate requirements, testing, and end-to-end certification submission management."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can Clarisco handle Nintendo Switch porting for a PC or console title?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our Nintendo Switch porting practice covers handheld and docked performance targeting, shader stutter elimination, Switch SDK integration, Joy-Con input implementation, memory footprint reduction, LotCheck compliance testing, and eShop submission management with experience across Unity and Unreal Engine Switch builds."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Do you manage the full certification submission process?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our certification practice manages the complete submission process with compliance documentation, submission build preparation, age rating filing, first-party submission form completion, and all platform holder communication and response management through to final approval."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Does Clarisco offer mobile game porting for PC or console titles?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our mobile game porting service adapts PC and console titles for iOS and Android by covering touch control redesign, mobile UI scaling, mobile GPU and memory optimization, texture compression conversion, App Store and Google Play compliance, and submission management through to live store approval."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can you port a mobile game to PC and add Steam integration?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our reverse porting practice takes successful iOS or Android titles to Steam by handling resolution and aspect ratio scaling, keyboard/mouse and controller input implementation, PC performance configuration across hardware tiers, Steam SDK integration, and Steam store submission including store page setup."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Do you offer cross-platform multiplayer integration as part of porting?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our cross-platform multiplayer integration covers Epic Online Services and platform-native online subsystem setup by enabling cross-play, shared matchmaking, cross-platform friends lists, and unified leaderboards across PC, console, and mobile from a single integration engagement."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can Clarisco establish cross-platform architecture for a new title in pre-production?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. For titles targeting simultaneous multi-platform launch, we establish cross-platform architecture in pre-production with input abstraction, platform-specific build pipeline, scalability system, and cross-play integration designed into the project from the start."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What engines does Clarisco's porting team work in?",
                                                                        a: "Our game porting studio works in Unity (all LTS versions), Unreal Engine 5 and UE4, Cocos2d-x, and Godot with engine-specific platform build pipeline expertise and SDK integration knowledge per target platform for each engine."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],

                                                                pricing: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How much does game porting cost?",
                                                                        a: "Simple Unity mobile-to-PC ports can start from $15K–$40K. Console ports typically range from $40K–$150K+. Nintendo Switch ports often run $50K–$120K+ due to optimization requirements. We provide a detailed cost breakdown after a technical assessment."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How long does a typical game port take to complete?",
                                                                        a: "A straightforward port to a similar platform (PC to Xbox) typically runs 16–20 weeks. Ports requiring significant performance optimization (PC to Nintendo Switch) typically run 20–28 weeks. Cross-platform architecture builds for new titles vary by scope."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Why does game porting take longer when the internal team owns it?",
                                                                        a: "Internal teams managing a port alongside primary development context-switch between the port and their main roadmap, producing both slower porting progress and slower primary development simultaneously. Certification cycles that generate rapid platform holder responses compound this when the internal team is mid-sprint on unrelated work."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is included in a game porting cost estimate from Clarisco?",
                                                                        a: "Our porting cost estimate includes technical assessment results, scope breakdown by platform feature and optimization task, team structure and size, milestone schedule with weekly deliverables, cost per phase, certification management scope, and IP transfer terms delivered as a single document before any engagement is signed."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does Clarisco price porting engagements?",
                                                                        a: "Game porting engagements are priced as fixed-scope or time-and-materials (flexible scope, monthly billing, suitable for complex ports where optimization scope is uncertain before assessment). We recommend the right model after the technical assessment."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What happens if the port fails certification on the first submission?",
                                                                        a: "Our certification practice is structured to minimize first-submission failures through systematic pre-submission compliance testing. If a submission is rejected, our team owns the response and remediation by preparing the response documentation and implementing required fixes."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Who owns the porting source code and platform configurations after delivery?",
                                                                        a: "All porting source code, SDK integration code, platform-specific build configuration, certification documentation, and build pipeline setup transfer entirely to the client at engagement completion. No licensing terms or dependency on Clarisco."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can Clarisco take over a port that a previous vendor started but didn't finish?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. We conduct a technical assessment of the existing partial port by reviewing what's complete, what's broken, and what the remaining scope is, then produce a revised plan and timeline before assuming ownership of the engagement. The assessment is completed before any commitment to a completion timeline or cost."
                                                                    }
                                                                ]
                                                            };

                                                            function createFaq(section, id) {
                                                                const container = document.getElementById(id);
                                                                faqData[section].forEach((item, index) => {
                                                                    const html = `<div class="accordion-item">
                                                                        <p class="accordion-header">
                                                                        <button class="accordion-button ${index !== 0 ? 'collapsed' : ''}" 
                                                                        data-bs-toggle="collapse" 
                                                                        data-bs-target="#${section}${index}">
                                                                        <span class="faq-icon"><i class="bi bi-book"></i></span>
                                                                        <span class="faq-title">${item.q}</span>
                                                                        </button>
                                                                        </p>
                                                                        <div id="${section}${index}" class="accordion-collapse collapse ${index === 0 ? 'show' : ''}"  data-bs-parent="#${id}">
                                                                        <div class="accordion-body">${item.a}</div>
                                                                        </div>
                                                                        </div>`;
                                                                    container.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend", html);
                                                                });
                                                            }
                                                            createFaq("general", "generalFaq");
                                                            createFaq("business", "businessFaq");
                                                            createFaq("pricing", "pricingFaq");
                                                        </script>

                                                        <script>
                                                            $(document).ready(function ($) {
                                                                //Check if an element was in a screen
                                                                function isScrolledIntoView(elem) {
                                                                    var docViewTop = $(window).scrollTop();
                                                                    var docViewBottom = docViewTop + $(window).height();
                                                                    var elemTop = $(elem).offset().top;
                                                                    var elemBottom = elemTop + $(elem).height();
                                                                    return ((elemBottom <= docViewBottom));
                                                                }
                                                                //Count up code
                                                                function countUp() {
                                                                    $('.counter').each(function () {
                                                                        var $this = $(this), // <- Don't touch this variable. It's pure magic.
                                                                            countTo = $this.attr('data-count');
